{
  "recorded": "2026-09-14",
  "codex_cli": "codex-cli 0.154.0 (managed standalone install at ~/.codex/packages/standalone; the Homebrew 0.145.0 remains installed)",
  "daemon": "codex app-server daemon start -> pid backend, socket ~/.codex/app-server-control/app-server-control.sock (srw------- in a 0700 directory)",
  "purpose": "Live proof for issue #42: a second JSON-RPC client (scripts/probe_app_server_daemon.py --watch) on the daemon socket while the user ran the TUI in Ghostty and asked for a request_user_input question, then answered it in the TUI.",
  "findings": [
    "The control socket speaks WebSocket over the Unix socket: an HTTP upgrade first, then one JSON-RPC message per text frame. A raw JSON line is closed without reply.",
    "The TUI (0.154.0, started as plain `codex` in a Ghostty tab) attaches to the daemon: thread/started arrived on the probe's connection and thread/loaded/list listed the session.",
    "item/tool/requestUserInput arrived on the probe's connection with threadId equal to the rollout session id and itemId equal to the rollout function_call call_id (call_zb49aiYiAuSSdKsNAkp5qYEG); the question ids and option labels matched the rollout arguments. It arrived without a successful thread/resume: server requests are delivered to every connected client.",
    "thread/resume on a thread whose rollout is not yet written is refused with -32600 'no rollout found'; the probe and Steer's client retry on the next poll.",
    "When the user answered in the TUI, the probe received serverRequest/resolved for request id 0, then thread/status/changed idle and turn/completed.",
    "The session's rollout session_meta says source: vscode and originator: steer-probe (the name of the first client that initialized the daemon), not cli. Steer now also classifies a session as CLI by its session-id Ghostty tab title.",
    "Closing the Ghostty tab does not end the session: the daemon still lists the thread as loaded, no thread/closed arrives for it, and no SessionEnd hook fires. Steer now ends a title-proved session when its title leaves Ghostty's inventory.",
    "Hooks still fire for daemon-attached sessions: SessionStart, UserPromptSubmit and Stop records arrived in Steer's events directory."
  ],
  "not_yet_proven": [
    "Answering through the probe (--answer) and through Steer's notch card; the user answered in the TUI in this round.",
    "Whether the desktop app attaches to the daemon (it still runs its own stdio app-server)."
  ],
